# carts/breakout — scripted walkthrough (M4 stage 4.0, Р20/Р25: re-planned for 160x90).
#
# The ball always serves straight up (main.cs, ServeAngle) from wherever the paddle sits, so
# this script steers each shot purely by repositioning the paddle *before* launch — it never
# needs to predict a paddle-bounce angle. Five rounds, and the run ends in a real terminal
# state: GameOver with all five lives spent.
#
#   rounds 0-3: walk the paddle across the four bottom-row brick columns left to right,
#               launching straight into each one in turn and stepping aside while the ball is
#               airborne so it is never caught — four bricks, four misses, bottom row cleared;
#   round 4:    launch from the middle, take one row-2 brick, step aside again — the fifth
#               miss spends the last life and the GAME OVER panel comes up.
#
# Everything below is arithmetic on main.cs's own constants at ScreenWidth/Height = 160x90
# (replays/README.md carries the full derivation). The numbers that changed with the screen:
# paddle width and brick width are both ScreenWidth/4 = 40 px (were 32), the paddle starts
# centred at x=60 (was 48) and its column stops are 0/40/80/120 (were 0/32/64/96), the paddle
# top is at y=83 (was 65), and one round trip of the ball is 104 ticks (was 68) because the
# ball has 18 px more air under the bricks to cross each way at BallSpeed = 1 px/tick.
#
# Grammar (quarp replay record --input-file): tick:buttons, entries separated by commas or
# newlines, '#' starts a comment. O is a *tap* (Btnp) — press then release — same as every
# turn in carts/snake's golden.input. L/R are held for a duration and then released. The
# cartridge sees entry N on its own tick N+1 (Ticks is incremented before Update), so the
# cartridge-scale ticks quoted below are one higher than the entry that caused them.

# round 0: paddle 60 -> 0 (30 ticks at 2 px/tick), launch, then paddle 0 -> 40 mid-flight.
# Brick (row 3, col 0) at tick 91; life 1 of 5 lost at tick 145.
5:L,35:,40:O,41:,50:R,70:,

# round 1: paddle already at 40 from the move above; launch, then paddle 40 -> 80 mid-flight.
# Brick (row 3, col 1) at tick 201; life 2 lost at tick 255.
150:O,151:,160:R,180:,

# round 2: paddle already at 80; launch, then paddle 80 -> 120 (its right stop) mid-flight.
# Brick (row 3, col 2) at tick 311; life 3 lost at tick 365.
260:O,261:,270:R,290:,

# round 3: paddle already at 120; launch — this shot clears the last bottom-row brick (row 3,
# col 3) at tick 421 — then paddle 120 -> 60, which is what turns the catch into the fourth
# miss (at x=120 the paddle would have caught this ball dead centre). Life 4 lost at tick 475.
370:O,371:,380:L,410:,

# round 4: paddle at 60, so the ball sits at x=78.5 and straddles brick columns 1 and 2. Row 3
# is gone by now, so the ball flies 5 ticks further up than in any earlier round and takes a
# row-2 brick at tick 536 instead — the flight time itself is the proof that the bottom row was
# cleared. Paddle 60 -> 0 gets out of the way; the fifth miss at tick 595 spends the last life
# and the run ends in GameOver.
480:O,481:,490:L,520:
